==============================================================================
ATTRIBUTION AND UPSTREAM PROVENANCE NOTICE
==============================================================================
1. Primary Baseline Method (CDA):
   The baseline architecture reconstructed in `src/anomaly_detection/models/baseline/`
   is based on the scientific paper:
     Ronglong Hu, Jizheng Yi, Xiaoyao Li, Aibin Chen, and Guangjie Han,
     "Efficient industrial anomaly detection via cross-scale distillation with
     enhanced feature compression," Pattern Recognition, Vol. 173, 112761, 2026.
     DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patcog.2025.112761
   and audited against the authors' reference repository:
     https://github.com/WHUer-cloud/CDA
   Note: The upstream repository `WHUer-cloud/CDA` does not specify an open-source
   LICENSE file as of commit `67224ca04d3aff03c97bdaad04aafb0b3a1ad74e`. No files
   from `WHUer-cloud/CDA` were copied verbatim into this repository; all modules
   were re-implemented cleanly with bug fixes for academic research and educational
   reproducibility in CS331. Any commercial use or redistribution of the CDA
   algorithm must respect the intellectual property rights of the original authors.

2. Benchmark Dataset Notice (MVTec AD):
   The MVTec Anomaly Detection dataset (Bergmann et al., CVPR 2019) is distributed
   by MVTec Software GmbH under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
   ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). Dataset files are never
   stored in or redistributed by this repository.
